---
// Honest limits · the things Rikiki deliberately doesn't do.
// Lists the rejected features so visitors can self-disqualify quickly.
---

<section id="limits" class="limits">
  <div class="inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">Honest limits</p>
    <h2>Not the right tool when…</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Rikiki is opinionated. Here's what it deliberately doesn't do,
      so you can rule it out fast.
    </p>

    <ul class="grid">
      <li>
        <strong>You want a WYSIWYG editor.</strong>
        Rikiki is write HTML, open in a browser. There's no builder UI,
        and there won't be one.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You need PowerPoint-style animation on shapes.</strong>
        Per-element timelines live in Keynote and Slidev, not here.
        You get slide-level transitions (fade, slide, zoom, flip). That's the lot.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You want a hosted SaaS.</strong>
        There isn't one. You host the static files yourself. S3, GitHub Pages,
        an nginx alias, whatever you've got.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You need PowerPoint export.</strong>
        Rikiki gives you HTML. <code>.pptx</code> output isn't on the roadmap.
        Export to PDF instead · <code>rikiki export</code>, or print from Chromium with backgrounds on.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You're allergic to Web Components.</strong>
        Custom Elements and Shadow DOM are the core. If your team policy
        bans them, walk away.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .limits {
    background: var(--rik-surface-page);
    padding: var(--rik-space-7) var(--rik-space-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rik-border-default);
  }
  .inner { max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--rik-text-default);
    color: var(--rik-surface-page);
    padding: 4px 10px;
    border-radius: var(--rik-radius-pill);
    font: 700 var(--rik-font-size-xs)/1 var(--rik-font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: var(--rik-space-3);
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--rik-font-display);
    font-size: var(--rik-font-size-mega);
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--rik-text-default);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0 0 var(--rik-space-3);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--rik-font-size-lead);
    color: var(--rik-text-default--muted);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: 0 0 var(--rik-space-6);
  }
  .grid {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--rik-space-3) var(--rik-space-5);
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .grid li {
    font-size: var(--rik-font-size-body);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--rik-text-default--muted);
    padding: var(--rik-space-3) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rik-border-default);
  }
  .grid li strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    color: var(--rik-text-default);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
  }
  .grid li code {
    font-family: var(--rik-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: rgba(42, 37, 32, 0.06);
    color: var(--rik-text-default);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
</style>
